[2026-11-19T11:53:15.155Z] [DEBUG] [rpc] safeoutputs→tools/call 1875b {"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"tools/call","params":{"arguments":{"body":"The owner's lead \"Chery sells an EV\" checks out, but it isn't a new car. Chery's only EV in Australia is the **E5**, which is the renamed **Omoda E5** already in the file as `omoda-e5-2024`. That entry's DC figure may now be wrong, and I couldn't confirm it with Chery: cheryaustralia.com.au and chery.com.au both failed with certificate or SSL errors.\n\n**What the file has now:** `omoda-e5-2024`: make \"Omoda\", 58 kWh usable (est.), 430 km WLTP, **80 kW DC** (est.). Source: \"Zecar listing (61.1 kWh, 430 km); peak, AC, 30-80% and usable est.\"\n\n**What recent reports say (MY26, single Ultimate grade, $37,990 drive-away):**\n- [TheBeep, MY26 article](https://thebeep.com.au/car-news/chery-e5-my26-price-specs-australia/): \"a full 30-to-80 per cent DC charge taking around 30 minutes at up to 130kW\", with a 58.9 kWh battery and 155 kW/288 Nm.\n- Zecar still lists 80 kW, with 10–80% in about 39 minutes, and a 61.1 kWh battery.\n- All sources agree on 430 km WLTP.\n\n**Decisions for the owner:**\n1. Should the entry's `make` show Chery? Its id must stay `omoda-e5-2024`. One option is a new `chery-e5-2026` entry for the MY26 car, with `untilYear` set on the Omoda one.\n2. Should the DC figure be 80 or 130 kW? If 130 kW is right for MY26, it would cut planned charging stops for current owners. I'd rather have Chery's own spec sheet before changing it.\n\nRelated lead not added this run: the **Leapmotor B05** is reported on sale since August 2026. Style: 56.2 kWh, 401 km WLTP. Design LR: 67.1 kWh, 482 km WLTP. Reports disagree on the Style's peak DC (156 vs 174 kW), and leapmotor.net/en-au failed with a certificate error. It stays a candidate until the maker page can be read.","title":"Omoda E5 is now sold as the Chery E5: DC figure may be out of date"},"name":"create_issue"}}
